From f267386612ff01c82c5512ffc9eba7ed58dab9f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Kudrin <clain@clain23.ru>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:29:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] s3: treat an R2 bucket lock refusal as final, read
 DeleteObjects per-key errors

- retryer: a 409 with code ObjectLockedByBucketPolicy is not retried (other
  409s are, as before); S3_MAX_RETRIES=15 with a 300 s cap retried it ~40 min.
- DeleteObjects reads the per-key error list of the 200 answer: a key the lock
  retains becomes storage.ObjectsRetainedError, any other per-key error fails.
- delete: retained objects are logged as "retained by bucket lock, not
  deleted" and the command exits 0 without "Objects deleted successfully".
- wal-push: an upload refused by the lock compares the stored segment; equal
  content is archived already (exit 0), different content fails at once.

Refs maestra-io/issues-maestra#1786
